{"id":"mahabharata-7-050","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":50,"title":"पञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 50 · Arjuna returns and learns of his son's death","summary":{"en":"At sunset, with the day's slaughter over, Arjuna returns from the Samshaptakas with Krishna and senses ill omens as the camp stands silent. Seeing the sorrowing Pandavas, he asks for Abhimanyu, and Krishna's heart is moved by his grief.","kn":"ಸೂರ್ಯಾಸ್ತದಲ್ಲಿ ದಿನದ ಹತ್ಯೆ ಮುಗಿದಾಗ ಅರ್ಜುನ ಕೃಷ್ಣನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಸಂಶಪ್ತಕರಿಂದ ಮರಳಿ ಮೌನ ಶಿಬಿರದಲ್ಲಿ ಅಪಶಕುನ ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುಃಖಿತ ಪಾಂಡವರನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯುವನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವನ ಶೋಕ ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಮನ ಕರಗಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"सूर्यास्त पर दिन का संहार समाप्त होने के बाद अर्जुन कृष्ण के साथ संशप्तकों से लौटते हैं और मौन शिविर में अपशकुन देखते हैं। शोकाकुल पाण्डवों को देखकर वे अभिमन्यु के बारे में पूछते हैं, और उनका शोक कृष्ण को द्रवित करता है।","te":"సూర్యాస్తమయంలో రోజు సంహారం ముగిశాక అర్జునుడు కృష్ణునితో సంశప్తకుల నుండి తిరిగి వచ్చి నిశ్శబ్ద శిబిరంలో దుశ్శకునాలు చూస్తాడు. దుఃఖితులైన పాండవులను చూసి అభిమన్యుని గురించి అడుగుతాడు; అతని శోకం కృష్ణుని కదిలిస్తుంది.","ta":"மாலையில் அன்றைய அழிவு முடிய, அர்ஜுனன் கண்ணனுடன் சம்சப்தகரிடமிருந்து திரும்பி அமைதியான பாசறையில் துர்நிமித்தம் காண்கிறான். துயருறும் பாண்டவரைக் கண்டு அபிமன்யுவைப் பற்றிக் கேட்கிறான்; அவன் துயரம் கண்ணனின் மனத்தை உருக்குகிறது.","ml":"സന്ധ്യയ്ക്ക് അന്നത്തെ കൂട്ടക്കൊല അവസാനിക്കുമ്പോൾ, സംശപ്തകരോടുള്ള യുദ്ധത്തിൽനിന്ന് കൃഷ്ണനോടൊപ്പം അർജുനൻ മടങ്ങിയെത്തുന്നു; പാളയം നിശ്ശബ്ദമായിരിക്കുന്നത് കണ്ട് അദ്ദേഹം ദുശ്ശകുനങ്ങൾ മനസ്സിലാക്കുന്നു. ദുഃഖിതരായ പാണ്ഡവരെ കണ്ട് അഭിമന്യുവിനെക്കുറിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെ ദുഃഖം കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ഹൃദയത്തെ അലിയിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.50; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"अभिमन्युवधपर्व","titleEn":"Abhimanyuvadha Parva (Slaying of Abhimanyu)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मिन्नहनि निर्वृत्ते घोरे प्राणभृतां क्षये ।\nआदित्येऽस्तंगते श्रीमान्संध्याकाल उपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that terrible day, which destroyed living beings, had ended, the sun had set and the glorious twilight hour had come."}},{"n":2,"text":"व्यपयातेषु सैन्येषु वासाय भरतर्षभ ।\nहत्वा संशप्तकव्रातान्दिव्यैरस्त्रैः कपिध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O best of the Bharatas, as the armies withdrew to rest, the one with the monkey banner, having killed the bands of Samshaptakas with divine weapons,"}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रायात्स्वशिबिरं जिष्णुर्जैत्रमास्थाय तं रथम् ।\nगच्छन्नेव च गोविन्दं सन्नकण्ठोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jishnu went toward his own camp, riding that victorious chariot, and as he went he spoke to Govinda with a choked throat."}},{"n":4,"text":"किं नु मे हृदयं त्रस्तं वाक्यं सज्जति केशव ।\nस्पन्दन्ति चाप्यनिष्टानि गात्रं सीदति चाच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Why is my heart afraid, Keshava, and why does my speech falter? Bad omens throb in my body, Achyuta, and my limbs sink.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"अनिष्टं चैव मे श्लिष्टं हृदयान्नापसर्पति ।\nभुवि यद्दिक्षु चाप्युग्रा उत्पातास्त्रासयन्ति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A feeling of misfortune clings to me and will not leave my heart. Fierce portents on earth and in every direction terrify me.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"बहुप्रकारा दृश्यन्ते सर्व एवाघशंसिनः ।\nअपि स्वस्ति भवेद्राज्ञः सामात्यस्य गुरोर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Many kinds of ill omens are seen, all announcing evil. Let there be well-being for the king, my elder, and his ministers.\""}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"व्यक्तं शिवं तव भ्रातुः सामात्यस्य भविष्यति ।\nमा शुचः किंचिदेवान्यत्तत्रानिष्टं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely your brother and his ministers will be well. Do not grieve. Perhaps some other minor misfortune has occurred there.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः संध्यामुपास्यैव वीरौ वीरावसादने ।\nकथयन्तौ रणे वृत्तं प्रयातौ रथमास्थितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two heroes, having offered the twilight prayers in a lonely spot, drove on in their chariot, speaking of what had happened in the battle."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः स्वशिबिरं प्राप्तौ हतानन्दं हतत्विषम् ।\nवासुदेवोऽर्जुनश्चैव कृत्वा कर्म सुदुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva and Arjuna, having done their very difficult work, reached their own camp, which had lost its joy and its lustre."}},{"n":10,"text":"ध्वस्ताकारं समालक्ष्य शिबिरं परवीरहा ।\nबीभत्सुरब्रवीत्कृष्णमस्वस्थहृदयस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the camp in a ruined state, Bibhatsu, slayer of enemy heroes, then spoke to Krishna, his heart uneasy."}},{"n":11,"text":"नाद्य नन्दन्ति तूर्याणि मङ्गल्यानि जनार्दन ।\nमिश्रा दुन्दुभिनिर्घोषैः शङ्खाश्चाडम्बरैः सह ।\nवीणा वा नाद्य वाद्यन्ते शम्यातालस्वनैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Janardana, today the auspicious instruments do not sound, mixed with the roar of drums, conches and horns, nor are lutes played with the sound of cymbals.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"मङ्गल्यानि च गीतानि न गायन्ति पठन्ति च ।\nस्तुतियुक्तानि रम्याणि ममानीकेषु बन्दिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The bards in my ranks do not sing or recite the auspicious, pleasing songs full of praise.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"योधाश्चापि हि मां दृष्ट्वा निवर्तन्ते ह्यधोमुखाः ।\nकर्माणि च यथापूर्वं कृत्वा नाभिवदन्ति माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even the warriors, when they see me, turn away with lowered faces. They do not speak to me as before, after doing their tasks.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"अपि स्वस्ति भवेदद्य भ्रातृभ्यो मम माधव ।\nन हि शुध्यति मे भावो दृष्ट्वा स्वजनमाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Madhava, let my brothers be well today. My heart is not at ease seeing my people so troubled.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अपि पाञ्चालराजस्य विराटस्य च मानद ।\nसर्वेषां चैव योधानां सामग्र्यं स्यान्ममाच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O giver of honour, Achyuta, let all be well with the Panchala king and Virata and all the warriors.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"न च मामद्य सौभद्रः प्रहृष्टो भ्रातृभिः सह ।\nरणादायान्तमुचितं प्रत्युद्याति हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Nor does Subhadra's son, joyous with his brothers, come smiling out to meet me as I return from battle, as is his custom.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"एवं संकथयन्तौ तौ प्रविष्टौ शिबिरं स्वकम् ।\nददृशाते भृशास्वस्थान्पाण्डवान्नष्टचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they talked thus, they entered their camp and saw the Pandavas deeply distressed and out of their senses."}},{"n":18,"text":"दृष्ट्वा भ्रातॄंश्च पुत्रांश्च विमना वानरध्वजः ।\nअपश्यंश्चैव सौभद्रमिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his brothers and sons, the one with the monkey banner was troubled, and not seeing Abhimanyu, he said these words."}},{"n":19,"text":"मुखवर्णोऽप्रसन्नो वः सर्वेषामेव लक्ष्यते ।\nन चाभिमन्युं पश्यामि न च मां प्रतिनन्दथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The faces of all of you look gloomy. I do not see Abhimanyu, and you do not greet me joyfully.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"मया श्रुतश्च द्रोणेन चक्रव्यूहो विनिर्मितः ।\nन च वस्तस्य भेत्तास्ति ऋते सौभद्रमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have heard that Drona has built a wheel formation, and no one among you can break it except Subhadra's son.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"न चोपदिष्टस्तस्यासीन्मयानीकविनिर्गमः ।\nकच्चिन्न बालो युष्माभिः परानीकं प्रवेशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I did not teach him how to come out of it. Surely you have not sent the boy into the enemy ranks?\""}},{"n":22,"text":"भित्त्वानीकं महेष्वासः परेषां बहुशो युधि ।\nकच्चिन्न निहतः शेते सौभद्रः परवीरहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely that great archer, slayer of enemy heroes, who broke through the enemy lines so often, does not lie slain?\""}},{"n":23,"text":"लोहिताक्षं महाबाहुं जातं सिंहमिवाद्रिषु ।\nउपेन्द्रसदृशं ब्रूत कथमायोधने हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me how he was killed in battle, the mighty-armed, red-eyed one, born like a lion among mountains, equal to Upendra.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"सुकुमारं महेष्वासं वासवस्यात्मजात्मजम् ।\nसदा मम प्रियं ब्रूत कथमायोधने हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me how he was killed in battle, the delicate great archer, grandson of Indra, always dear to me.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"वार्ष्णेयीदयितं शूरं मया सततलालितम् ।\nअम्बायाश्च प्रियं नित्यं कोऽवधीत्कालचोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who, driven by Time, killed that hero, beloved of Vrishni's daughter, whom I always cherished, and ever dear to his mother?\""}},{"n":26,"text":"सदृशो वृष्णिसिंहस्य केशवस्य महात्मनः ।\nविक्रमश्रुतमाहात्म्यैः कथमायोधने हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He was equal to Keshava, the great-souled lion of the Vrishnis, in prowess, learning and greatness. How was he killed in battle?\""}},{"n":27,"text":"सुभद्रायाः प्रियं नित्यं द्रौपद्याः केशवस्य च ।\nयदि पुत्रं न पश्यामि यास्यामि यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He was always dear to Subhadra, Draupadi and Keshava. If I do not see my son, I shall go to Yama's abode.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"मृदुकुञ्चितकेशान्तं बालं बालमृगेक्षणम् ।\nमत्तद्विरदविक्रान्तं शालपोतमिवोद्गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A boy with soft curling hair and eyes like a fawn's, striding like a rutting elephant, risen like a young sala tree.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"स्मिताभिभाषिणं दान्तं गुरुवाक्यकरं सदा ।\nबाल्येऽप्यबालकर्माणं प्रियवाक्यममत्सरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He spoke with a smile, was self-controlled, always obeyed his elders, did a man's deeds though a child, spoke kindly, and was free of envy.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"महोत्साहं महाबाहुं दीर्घराजीवलोचनम् ।\nभक्तानुकम्पिनं दान्तं न च नीचानुसारिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Full of energy, mighty-armed, long-eyed like a lotus, kind to those devoted to him, self-controlled, and never following the base.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"कृतज्ञं ज्ञानसंपन्नं कृतास्त्रमनिवर्तिनम् ।\nयुद्धाभिनन्दिनं नित्यं द्विषतामघवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Grateful, learned, skilled in weapons, never retreating, always delighting in battle, a raiser of the sorrow of his enemies.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"स्वेषां प्रियहिते युक्तं पितॄणां जयगृद्धिनम् ।\nन च पूर्वप्रहर्तारं संग्रामे नष्टसंभ्रमम् ।\nयदि पुत्रं न पश्यामि यास्यामि यमसादनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Devoted to the welfare and pleasure of his own people and to his elders, eager for victory, never the first to strike, never losing his composure in battle. If I do not see my son, I shall go to Yama's abode.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"सुललाटं सुकेशान्तं सुभ्र्वक्षिदशनच्छदम् ।\nअपश्यतस्तद्वदनं का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With his fair brow, hair, brows, eyes, teeth and lips. Without seeing that face, what peace is there for my heart?\""}},{"n":34,"text":"तन्त्रीस्वनसुखं रम्यं पुंस्कोकिलसमध्वनिम् ।\nअशृण्वतः स्वनं तस्य का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"His voice was sweet as the sound of strings, like a male cuckoo's. Without hearing his voice, what peace is there for my heart?\""}},{"n":35,"text":"रूपं चाप्रतिरूपं तत्त्रिदशेष्वपि दुर्लभम् ।\nअपश्यतोऽद्य वीरस्य का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"His form was matchless, hard to find even among the gods. Without seeing that hero today, what peace is there for my heart?\""}},{"n":36,"text":"अभिवादनदक्षं तं पितॄणां वचने रतम् ।\nनाद्याहं यदि पश्यामि का शान्तिर्हृदयस्य मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He was skilled in saluting and devoted to his elders' words. If I do not see him today, what peace is there for my heart?\""}},{"n":37,"text":"सुकुमारः सदा वीरो महार्हशयनोचितः ।\nभूमावनाथवच्छेते नूनं नाथवतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ever delicate, accustomed to costly beds, that hero, best of those who have protectors, surely lies on the ground like one with none.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"शयानं समुपासन्ति यं पुरा परमस्त्रियः ।\nतमद्य विप्रविद्धाङ्गमुपासन्त्यशिवाः शिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He whom the foremost women once attended as he lay down, surely today, with his limbs thrown about, is attended by inauspicious jackals.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"यः पुरा बोध्यते सुप्तः सूतमागधबन्दिभिः ।\nबोधयन्त्यद्य तं नूनं श्वापदा विकृतैः स्वरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He who was once awakened from sleep by charioteers, bards and panegyrists is surely awakened today by beasts of prey with hideous cries.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"छत्रच्छायासमुचितं तस्य तद्वदनं शुभम् ।\nनूनमद्य रजोध्वस्तं रणे रेणुः करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"That fair face, used to the shade of a parasol, surely the dust of battle has stained today.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"हा पुत्रकावितृप्तस्य सततं पुत्रदर्शने ।\nभाग्यहीनस्य कालेन यथा मे नीयसे बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Alas, my little son, I was never satisfied with seeing you, and now unlucky as I am, Time carries you away from me by force.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"साद्य संयमनी नूनं सदा सुकृतिनां गतिः ।\nस्वभाभिर्भासिता रम्या त्वयात्यर्थं विराजते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely that Samyamani, always the goal of the virtuous, shines brightly today with its own radiance, made lovely by you.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"नूनं वैवस्वतश्च त्वा वरुणश्च प्रियातिथिः ।\nशतक्रतुर्धनेशश्च प्राप्तमर्चन्त्यभीरुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely Vaivasvata, Varuna, Indra of the hundred sacrifices and the lord of wealth, who love guests, honour you, the fearless one who has come.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"एवं विलप्य बहुधा भिन्नपोतो वणिग्यथा ।\nदुःखेन महताविष्टो युधिष्ठिरमपृच्छत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lamenting thus in many ways, like a merchant whose ship has broken, and overcome with great grief, he asked Yudhishthira."}},{"n":45,"text":"कच्चित्स कदनं कृत्वा परेषां पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nस्वर्गतोऽभिमुखः संख्ये युध्यमानो नरर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Son of Pandu, did that bull among men, after slaughtering the enemy, go to heaven facing them as he fought in battle?\""}},{"n":46,"text":"स नूनं बहुभिर्यत्तैर्युध्यमानो नरर्षभैः ।\nअसहायः सहायार्थी मामनुध्यातवान्ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely, fighting many bull-like warriors who were trying to kill him, he was alone and wished for help, and surely thought of me.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"पीड्यमानः शरैर्बालस्तात साध्वभिधाव माम् ।\nइति विप्रलपन्मन्ये नृशंसैर्बहुभिर्हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I think he cried out in distress, 'Father, run to me quickly,' as he was struck down by many cruel men, tormented by arrows.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"अथ वा मत्प्रसूतश्च स्वस्रीयो माधवस्य च ।\nसुभद्रायां च संभूतो नैवं वक्तुमिहार्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Or else, born of me, a nephew of Madhava and son of Subhadra, he would not speak such words.\""}},{"n":49,"text":"वज्रसारमयं नूनं हृदयं सुदृढं मम ।\nअपश्यतो दीर्घबाहुं रक्ताक्षं यन्न दीर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My heart must be made of diamond-hard iron and be very firm, for it does not break though I cannot see my long-armed, red-eyed son.\""}},{"n":50,"text":"कथं बाले महेष्वासे नृशंसा मर्मभेदिनः ।\nस्वस्रीये वासुदेवस्य मम पुत्रेऽक्षिपञ्शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How could those cruel men, who pierce vitals, shoot arrows at a boy and great archer, Vasudeva's nephew and my son?\""}},{"n":51,"text":"यो मां नित्यमदीनात्मा प्रत्युद्गम्याभिनन्दति ।\nउपयान्तं रिपून्हत्वा सोऽद्य मां किं न पश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He who always came to meet me undismayed and welcomed me when I came back after killing enemies, why does he not see me today?\""}},{"n":52,"text":"नूनं स पतितः शेते धरण्यां रुधिरोक्षितः ।\nशोभयन्मेदिनीं गात्रैरादित्य इव पातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely he lies fallen on the ground covered in blood, adorning the earth with his limbs like a fallen sun.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"रणे विनिहतं श्रुत्वा शोकार्ता वै विनंक्ष्यति ।\nसुभद्रा वक्ष्यते किं मामभिमन्युमपश्यती ।\nद्रौपदी चैव दुःखार्ते ते च वक्ष्यामि किं न्वहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing him killed in battle, Subhadra will die, tormented with grief. What will she say to me when she does not see Abhimanyu? What shall I say to Draupadi, afflicted with grief, and to the others?\""}},{"n":54,"text":"वज्रसारमयं नूनं हृदयं यन्न यास्यति ।\nसहस्रधा वधूं दृष्ट्वा रुदतीं शोककर्शिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely my heart is made of diamond-hard iron, since it does not split into a thousand pieces on seeing my daughter-in-law weeping, wasted with grief.\""}},{"n":55,"text":"हृष्टानां धार्तराष्ट्राणां सिंहनादो मया श्रुतः ।\nयुयुत्सुश्चापि कृष्णेन श्रुतो वीरानुपालभन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I heard the lion-roar of the joyful sons of Dhritarashtra, and Yuyutsu was also heard by Krishna, reproaching the heroes.\""}},{"n":56,"text":"अशक्नुवन्तो बीभत्सुं बालं हत्वा महारथाः ।\nकिं नदध्वमधर्मज्ञाः पार्थे वै दृश्यतां बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'Why do you shout, you who do not know dharma, you great chariot-warriors who killed a boy because you could not face Bibhatsu? Let your strength be shown against Partha.'\""}},{"n":57,"text":"किं तयोर्विप्रियं कृत्वा केशवार्जुनयोर्मृधे ।\nसिंहवन्नदत प्रीताः शोककाल उपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'What wrong did you do to Keshava and Arjuna in battle, that you roar happily like lions when your time of mourning has come?'\""}},{"n":58,"text":"आगमिष्यति वः क्षिप्रं फलं पापस्य कर्मणः ।\nअधर्मो हि कृतस्तीव्रः कथं स्यादफलश्चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"'The fruit of your sinful deed will soon come to you. How could such a terrible wrong be fruitless for long?'\""}},{"n":59,"text":"इति तान्प्रति भाषन्वै वैश्यापुत्रो महामतिः ।\nअपायाच्छस्त्रमुत्सृज्य कोपदुःखसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So saying to them, the wise son of the Vaishya woman threw down his weapon and left, filled with anger and sorrow."}},{"n":60,"text":"किमर्थमेतन्नाख्यातं त्वया कृष्ण रणे मम ।\nअधक्ष्यं तानहं सर्वांस्तदा क्रूरान्महारथान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna, why did you not tell me this in the battle? I would have burned all those cruel great chariot-warriors then.\""}},{"n":61,"text":"निगृह्य वासुदेवस्तं पुत्राधिभिरभिप्लुतम् ।\nमैवमित्यब्रवीत्कृष्णस्तीव्रशोकसमन्वितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva took hold of him, overwhelmed by grief for his son, and said to him, \"Not so,\" as he himself was filled with deep grief."}},{"n":62,"text":"सर्वेषामेष वै पन्थाः शूराणामनिवर्तिनाम् ।\nक्षत्रियाणां विशेषेण येषां युद्धेन जीविका ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is the path of all brave men who never turn back, and especially of kshatriyas, whose livelihood is war.\""}},{"n":63,"text":"एषा वै युध्यमानानां शूराणामनिवर्तिनाम् ।\nविहिता धर्मशास्त्रज्ञैर्गतिर्गतिमतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This, best of those who go well, has been laid down by the knowers of dharma as the goal of brave men who fight and never retreat.\""}},{"n":64,"text":"ध्रुवं युद्धे हि मरणं शूराणामनिवर्तिनाम् ।\nगतः पुण्यकृतां लोकानभिमन्युर्न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Death in battle is certain for brave men who never turn back. Abhimanyu has gone to the worlds of the righteous, without doubt.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"एतच्च सर्ववीराणां काङ्क्षितं भरतर्षभ ।\nसंग्रामेऽभिमुखा मृत्युं प्राप्नुयामेति मानद ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This, best of the Bharatas, is the wish of all heroes, O giver of honour: to meet death facing the enemy in battle.\""}},{"n":66,"text":"स च वीरान्रणे हत्वा राजपुत्रान्महाबलान् ।\nवीरैराकाङ्क्षितं मृत्युं संप्राप्तोऽभिमुखो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having killed mighty princes in battle, he met the death that heroes long for, facing the enemy.\""}},{"n":67,"text":"मा शुचः पुरुषव्याघ्र पूर्वैरेष सनातनः ।\nधर्मकृद्भिः कृतो धर्मः क्षत्रियाणां रणे क्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Do not grieve, tiger among men. This is the ancient dharma of kshatriyas, done by earlier righteous men: to perish in battle.\""}},{"n":68,"text":"इमे ते भ्रातरः सर्वे दीना भरतसत्तम ।\nत्वयि शोकसमाविष्टे नृपाश्च सुहृदस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Best of the Bharatas, all your brothers, the kings and your friends are downcast while you are overcome with grief.\""}},{"n":69,"text":"एतांस्त्वं वचसा साम्ना समाश्वासय मानद ।\nविदितं वेदितव्यं ते न शोकं कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Comfort them with gentle words, giver of honour. You know what is to be known, and you should not grieve.\""}},{"n":70,"text":"एवमाश्वासितः पार्थः कृष्णेनाद्भुतकर्मणा ।\nततोऽब्रवीत्तदा भ्रातॄन्सर्वान्पार्थः सगद्गदान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus comforted by Krishna of wondrous deeds, Partha then spoke to all his brothers, his voice choked."}},{"n":71,"text":"स दीर्घबाहुः पृथ्वंसो दीर्घराजीवलोचनः ।\nअभिमन्युर्यथा वृत्तः श्रोतुमिच्छाम्यहं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I want to hear how Abhimanyu, long-armed and broad-shouldered, with long lotus eyes, fought and fell.\""}},{"n":72,"text":"सनागस्यन्दनहयान्द्रक्ष्यध्वं निहतान्मया ।\nसंग्रामे सानुबन्धांस्तान्मम पुत्रस्य वैरिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You will see them killed by me in battle, with their elephants, chariots and horses and all their followers, those enemies of my son.\""}},{"n":73,"text":"कथं च वः कृतास्त्राणां सर्वेषां शस्त्रपाणिनाम् ।\nसौभद्रो निधनं गच्छेद्वज्रिणापि समागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How could Subhadra's son die, even when meeting the wielder of the thunderbolt, while you all, skilled in weapons, stood with weapons in hand?\""}},{"n":74,"text":"यद्येवमहमज्ञास्यमशक्तान्रक्षणे मम ।\nपुत्रस्य पाण्डुपाञ्चालान्मया गुप्तो भवेत्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I had known that Pandavas and Panchalas were unable to protect my son, I would have protected him myself.\""}},{"n":75,"text":"कथं च वो रथस्थानां शरवर्षाणि मुञ्चताम् ।\nनीतोऽभिमन्युर्निधनं कदर्थीकृत्य वः परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How was Abhimanyu brought to his death by the enemy, who treated you as nothing, while you stood on your chariots shooting showers of arrows?\""}},{"n":76,"text":"अहो वः पौरुषं नास्ति न च वोऽस्ति पराक्रमः ।\nयत्राभिमन्युः समरे पश्यतां वो निपातितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Ah, you have no manliness, you have no prowess, if Abhimanyu was struck down in battle while you watched.\""}},{"n":77,"text":"आत्मानमेव गर्हेयं यदहं वः सुदुर्बलान् ।\nयुष्मानाज्ञाय निर्यातो भीरूनकृतनिश्रमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I can only blame myself, for I went away relying on you, who are very weak, cowardly and unwearied by effort.\""}},{"n":78,"text":"आहोस्विद्भूषणार्थाय वर्मशस्त्रायुधानि वः ।\nवाचश्च वक्तुं संसत्सु मम पुत्रमरक्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Or are your armour, weapons and arms only for show, and your words only for speaking in assemblies, since you did not protect my son?\""}},{"n":79,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो वाक्यं तिष्ठंश्चापवरासिमान् ।\nन स्माशक्यत बीभत्सुः केनचित्प्रसमीक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, he stood with his bow and fine sword, and no one could look at Bibhatsu."}},{"n":80,"text":"तमन्तकमिव क्रुद्धं निःश्वसन्तं मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nपुत्रशोकाभिसंतप्तमश्रुपूर्णमुखं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was angry like Death, sighing again and again, burning with grief for his son, his face full of tears."}},{"n":81,"text":"नाभिभाष्टुं शक्नुवन्ति द्रष्टुं वा सुहृदोऽर्जुनम् ।\nअन्यत्र वासुदेवाद्वा ज्येष्टाद्वा पाण्डुनन्दनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"None of his friends could speak to Arjuna or look at him, except Vasudeva or his elder, the son of Pandu."}},{"n":82,"text":"सर्वास्ववस्थासु हितावर्जुनस्य मनोनुगौ ।\nबहुमानात्प्रियत्वाच्च तावेनं वक्तुमर्हतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were his well-wishers in every state and followed his mind, and out of respect and affection those two could speak to him."}},{"n":83,"text":"ततस्तं पुत्रशोकेन भृशं पीडितमानसम् ।\nराजीवलोचनं क्रुद्धं राजा वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king spoke to the lotus-eyed Arjuna, who was angry and deeply tormented by grief for his son."}}]}]}